 something else shows up as drift.
 
+## Plugin client inventories (community compatibility extension)
+
+A package may declare `magpie.agentInstances` as the home-relative path of
+a plugin-owned JSON inventory. Version 1 contains `includeBase` (default
+true), optional `baseName`, and `instances`: `{id, name, config, dir}`.
+Config and directory paths relative to the inventory are resolved there.
+Each client reuses the module's connect hook, format and model keys, but
+gets its own model visibility, gateway identity, stash and native Agent row.
+No additional plugin entry or generated module is installed. Startup and
+Library paths are not cloned. Duplicate IDs/config paths and malformed or
+oversized inventories are refused. Inventory timestamps participate in
+the existing agent reload stamp.
+
+For splitting an existing shared client, `inherit: true` imports the base
+row's visibility and a matching copied bridge once. A separate stash marker
+prevents a later disconnect from importing it again. Existing target model
+filters, including an empty picked list, take precedence. UnwirePlugin
+restores every client and any leftover stash of the package. Disconnect
+previews copy the inventory too, resolve relative paths under the copied
+home, and relocate absolute home paths; inventories outside home have no
+preview. Tests: `TestPluginInstancesInheritOnceAndDisconnectIndependently`,
+`TestPluginInstancePreviewUsesOnlyCopiedFiles`, `TestInstanceInventory*`.
+
